    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d443">

                <pb facs="0615" n="329" xml:id="pg329"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 341.115Am319/104</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Page</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-01-03">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">January 3, 1916</hi>
                        </date>.<lb/>[<hi rendition="#italic">Received 2.50 p. m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3493. Your 2603, December 20, and 2645 and 2646, 29, re <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Kankakee</hi>.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d443-f1"/> Foreign Office informs me
                    that it is now in receipt of communication from Admiralty from which it appears
                    that this vessel was captured by British naval forces as far back as October 31
                    last, and that she has been conveyed to Gibraltar where she is at present on the
                    point of arrival.</p>
                <closer>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Embassy</hi>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
